TechCrunch reported: the board put Matt on leave against his will;
One person guessed his Burning Man trip helped them time it well.
Mark Davies, the CFO, took charge in Matt’s stead;
For thirty-three hours and twenty minutes, he led.

But Matt seemingly declined to depart as they had planned;
He booted other admins from Slack and said he was in command.
Then Matt pushed out the board and restored himself as chief;
The directors’ time in charge had been remarkably brief.

